libgcobol: wire libxml2 into the gcobol link spec; keep build paths out

Companion to 0012 (which made libxml2 optional) for the case where the
target DOES provide libxml2 (mcm bundles a minimal static libxml2.a in the
sysroot for COBOL XML PARSE; see litecross obj_libxml2).  Two fixes:

  * libgcobol.spec gains @LIBXML2SPEC@ (-lxml2 when libgcobol was built
    with libxml2, empty otherwise).  Upstream's spec never links libxml2,
    so on a static-by-default toolchain every `gcobol -static` program
    using XML PARSE dies with undefined xml* references.  Dynamic links
    are unaffected (libgcobol.so already carries the dependency), as are
    programs that never pull xmlparse.o from libgcobol.a.

  * The --with-target-libxml2 flags path no longer puts -L<libdir> into
    LIBXML2_LIBS.  libtool copies -L flags into the installed
    libgcobol.la (dependency_libs); for a cross build that directory is
    an absolute build-tree path, i.e. a raw-path leak into the shipped
    toolchain (stage2/package gate step 3 rejects it).  The target
    compiler already searches the (build) sysroot the library lives in,
    so plain -lxml2 resolves.

The shipped configure is hand-edited in sync with configure.ac because
litecross does not autoreconf (same practice as 0012).

--- a/libgcobol/configure.ac	2026-08-16 21:59:11.856368680 +0200
+++ b/libgcobol/configure.ac	2026-08-16 21:59:31.058892321 +0200
@@ -335,7 +335,12 @@
       AC_MSG_ERROR([no multilib path ($mldir) found in --with-target-libxml2-lib])
     fi
     LIBXML2_CPPFLAGS="-I$libxml2_inc_dir"
-    LIBXML2_LIBS="-L$libxml2_lib_dir -lxml2"
+    dnl mcm: no -L$libxml2_lib_dir here.  libtool copies -L flags into the
+    dnl installed libgcobol.la (dependency_libs), and for a cross build the
+    dnl configured lib dir is an absolute build-tree path -- a path leak into
+    dnl the shipped toolchain.  The target compiler already searches the
+    dnl (build) sysroot the library is installed in, so plain -lxml2 resolves.
+    LIBXML2_LIBS="-lxml2"
     AC_MSG_RESULT([found])
   fi
 else
@@ -345,6 +350,19 @@
 AC_SUBST(LIBXML2_CPPFLAGS)
 AC_SUBST(LIBXML2_LIBS)
 
+dnl mcm: gcobol links user programs against libgcobol via libgcobol.spec.
+dnl When libgcobol was built with libxml2, a *static* user link (-static,
+dnl -static-pie) must append -lxml2 after -lgcobol or every program using
+dnl XML PARSE fails with undefined xml* references; upstream's spec never
+dnl adds it.  Harmless for dynamic links (libgcobol.so already carries the
+dnl dependency) and for programs that never pull xmlparse.o from the archive.
+if test "x$LIBXML2_LIBS" != x; then
+  LIBXML2SPEC=-lxml2
+else
+  LIBXML2SPEC=
+fi
+AC_SUBST(LIBXML2SPEC)
+
